d.rep("### 5.3 The gate: contract per PR, wiring order, one attempt (S-1 and S-2a)", """### 5.2b What ends the run when the gate refuses, in S-1 (readiness major 1)

**Decision: S-1 ships four small handlers and keeps the per-attempt window check.** Why not move the window check in `chat` to S-2a: the point of S-1 is a date that no retry loop can cross. Without a handler, the first call after the date would raise out of `Runtime.handle`, leave the run in `WORKING` until `tick` finds it, and end the replay and the `gate` command with a traceback. The four sites that call a model are listed in F8; each gets its end here:

| Site | S-1 handling | Test |
|---|---|---|
| main call, `runtime/agent_loop.py:425` | a new `except SpendRefused as exc:` beside `except ProviderError` (`runtime/agent_loop.py:432`): `self._note(run, "llm", "chat", result="stopped", error_code=exc.code)`, then `return self._to(run, S.NEEDS_PERSON, f"limits.{exc.code}")`: the same state and reason string as `_limits_stop`, no card. S-2a deletes it when `handle` is split and `_wall_stop` posts the card (5.5) | E0-S1-3(c): the run ends `NEEDS_PERSON` with `limits.window_ended`, never `WORKING` |
| screen and judge (`runtime/agent_loop.py:310`, `guard/judge.py:72`) | no edit: `injection_check` turns every exception, `SpendRefused` included, into a flagged verdict `guard_unavailable` (`guard/injection.py:85-101`), so the run stops as a flagged screen: the wrong reason text, a safe state; S-2a gives it the right reason (5.5) | E0-S1-3(d) |
| replay, `k1b/loop.py:176` | a new `except SpendRefused:` before `except ProviderError`: `out.status, out.stop_reason, out.halt = "error", "spend_refused", "aborted"; return out` (without it `run_case` raises, security minor F10) | E0-S1-3(e): one replayed case ends with that status and no exception |
| `evals.py:73` through `hadavin-sdk gate`; `extract.py:47` | the `gate` branch of `main` (`src/hadavin_sdk/cli.py:146`) catches `SpendRefused`, prints `spend refused: <code>` on stderr and exits 2; `extract()` lets the refusal rise (no caller outside tests; its docstring says so) | E0-S1-3(f) |

### 5.3 The gate: contract per PR, wiring order, one attempt (S-1 and S-2a)""")
d.rep("`window_ended, daily_budget, monthly_budget, call_too_large, prompt_too_large,", "`window_ended, daily_budget, monthly_budget, call_too_large, call_retry_budget, prompt_too_large,")
